# S E R A P H I C   T E C H N O L O G I E S   -   S I G N A T U R E   G U I D E

This document defines the professional visual and technical metadata standards for the **Seraphic Technologies** codebase. All project files must adhere to these standards to ensure clarity, maintainability, and professional engineering quality.

---

## The Professional Signature

The signature block provides critical file metadata and technical context for developers.

### Template for Source Code (`.rs`, `.ts`, `.py`, `.js`)

```text
/*
 *  S E R A P H I C   T E C H N O L O G I E S
 * ╭──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
 * │ FILE ID: SER-0x[HASH] | REVISION: 2026.04.20                             │
 * │ PATH: [relative/path/to/file]                                            │
 * ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
 * │ DESCRIPTION: [High-level technical summary of the file's function]       │
 * │ COMPONENTS:  [Primary modules, classes, or exported functions]           │
 * ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
 * │ TECHNICAL NOTES: [Specific implementation details or performance goals]  │
 * ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
 *   SERAPHIC TECH - Precision Engineering
 */
```

### Template for Markdown (`.md`)

```text
<pre>
  S E R A P H I C   T E C H N O L O G I E S
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ FILE ID: SER-DOC-0x[HASH] | REVISION: 2026.04.20                           │
│ PATH: [filename.md]                                                        │
├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ DESCRIPTION: [Objective of this documentation]                             │
│ COMPONENTS:  [Key sections and knowledge items]                            │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
  SERAPHIC TECH - Specialized Technical Documentation
</pre>
```

---

## Documentation Standards

All public-facing code should use standard professional documentation comments.

**Example (Rust):**
```rust
/// Calculates the geometric resonant harmonic of the input signal.
///
/// # Arguments
/// * `input` - The raw signal value to process.
fn calculate_harmonic(input: f64) -> f64 { ... }
```

---

## Formatting and Terminology

- **Date Format**: `YYYY.MM.DD` (e.g., `2026.04.20`).
- **File IDs**: `SER-0x[8-character hash]` derived from the file path.
- **Terminology**: Avoid non-technical, mystical, or spiritual language. Use "Revision" instead of "Ascension", "Specification" instead of "Mandate", and "Technical Notes" instead of "Seraphic Notes".

